%%%%%Hand 6Hand 5
https://tinyurl.com/2a84fd99
qx|A5|st||rh||ah|Board 5 IMPs   -   July 17, 2024|pn|hondo717,IraCT,Sputniks,danpsych|
md|4SA63HA987D42CKT32,SKT4HK653D865C765,SQJHQJ42DKQJTCJ94,S98752HTDA973CAQ8|sv|e|
mb|P?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I hate holding flat 11 point hands. I will never open a flat 11 point if it doesn't meet the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule Of 20^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 76 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Having said that, I do recommend that you use "Bergen Adjusted Points" to calculate the "points" you use in Rule of 20 calculations. |
PG| ***** 77 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That means you use the Bergen Starting Point rules other than length (which is accounted for by “the length of your two longest suits”) - HCP, quality suits, dubious shortness, and adjust 3 - to calculate your points. |
PG| ***** 78 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If I did that, my hand would be worth 12 "points" because I have 11 HCP plus I can add 1 point for having 3 aces/tens and no queens/jacks (adjust3). So my hand technically meets the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at|. But I hate flat 11 HCP hands so much I still pass.|
PG| ***** 79 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|1D?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If not vulnerable, despite the weak spade suit, I might bid 1@S with the East hand. Do it whenever you can lay claim to the spade suit in a hand where both sides have approximately equal points. That is good, because holding spades means you can outbid the opponents while not going up to one level higher.|
PG| ***** 80 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|On the other hand, I agree with pass by East because of the vulnerability, particularly at IMPs. In Match Points, where being aggressive in part score hands often pays off, I might still bid 1@S, though, it is definitely very risky.|
PG| ***** 81 ***** |


mb|P|mb|1H|mb|P|mb|2H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|My hand is now worth 13 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=declarerpoints,Bergen Declarer Points^*N|CP||FP||at|. It has 11 HCP, 1 point for 3 aces/tens and no queens and jacks, and 1 point for the side 4 card club suit. In Match Points I probably only bid 3@H because as I said I don't love flat hands with 11 HCP and I tend to be conservative with an 8 card fit.|
PG| ***** 82 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|But in IMPs I should bid 4@H because you should aggressively bid games in IMPs. BTW, for those interested, I have a very good lesson on the difference in tactics between Match Points and IMPs. Click  |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=scoring,HERE^*N|CP||FP||at|, to see it.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 83 ***** |


mb|4H|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 84 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|
pc|S4|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I would have led a club. Leading away from a king is risky, as this hand illustrates.|
PG| ***** 85 ***** |


pc|SJ|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I am likely to take 3 hearts with length along 1 extra heart with a ruff, 2 spades, and 3 diamond. So I need one club trick.|
PG| ***** 86 ***** |


